<Project Sdk="Microsoft.NET.Sdk">

  <PropertyGroup>
    <RootNamespace>Harness.Wire</RootNamespace>
    <AssemblyName>Harness.Wire</AssemblyName>
  </PropertyGroup>

  <!--
    The client half of the walking skeleton: write vector, raise start bool, poll, read results
    (2.4), the inert establish and its two-part verify (2.5), and the version register's
    post-download check (2.6).

    NModbus, NOT raw sockets. Phase 1 used raw sockets on purpose — the question there was whether
    `MB_SERVER` tears a multi-register write, and a library that retried or split a request could
    have been read as the PLC tearing. Phase 2 is not that experiment.

    Everything above the transport is driven through IRegisterTransport, so the whole sequence —
    every refusal, the quiescence check, the later-scan commit rule, the settling window — is
    testable with no device and no socket.
  -->
  <ItemGroup>
    <PackageReference Include="NModbus" />
  </ItemGroup>

  <ItemGroup>
    <ProjectReference Include="..\Harness.Map\Harness.Map.csproj" />
  </ItemGroup>

</Project>
